{"id":"chatcmpl-6f2c36df-b7f1-4fd1-90b3-c67dbe8187a5","object":"chat.completion","created":1795246523,"model":"deepseek-v4.1-flash","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","reasoning_content":"","content":"```json\n{\n  \"highlights\": \"When a visual QA tool returns ambiguous or truncated output, the successful strategy was to re-query with a more specific, structured question that forces explicit description of the relevant anatomy and laterality cues. The agent also adapted its question to the identified image view (lateral vs frontal), using view-specific landmarks (e.g., gastric bubble) to disambiguate left vs right. Final answer selection relied on the tool's explicit laterality statement rather than inference.\",\n  \"patterns\": [\n    \"If a tool response is truncated or ambiguous, re-issue a more specific query that demands explicit description of the target feature and its laterality.\",\n    \"Adapt follow-up questions to the identified image view, using view-specific anatomical landmarks to resolve left/right ambiguity.\",\n    \"Use a two-stage tool strategy: first confirm image orientation/view, then ask targeted questions that leverage that orientation.\",\n    \"Prefer the tool's explicit laterality/label output over the agent's own inference when forming the final answer.\"\n  ],\n  \"playbooks\": {\n    \"Medical imaging QA\": \"First confirm image view/orientation, then ask targeted questions about specific structures and laterality; use landmarks (e.g., gastric bubble) to disambiguate sides.\",\n    \"Tool-output recovery\": \"When output is truncated or vague, re-query with a structured prompt requesting explicit descriptions rather than yes/no answers.\",\n    \"Ambiguous laterality resolution\": \"Ask the tool to state which side is affected and cite a confirming landmark before committing to an answer.\"\n  },\n  \"checklists\": [\n    \"Confirm the image view (frontal vs lateral) before interpreting laterality-dependent findings.\",\n    \"Verify the tool explicitly states the affected side and a supporting landmark before selecting the answer.\"\n  ]\n}\n```"},"finish_reason":"stop","logprobs":null}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":495,"total_tokens":863,"completion_tokens":368,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0,"image_tokens":0,"text_tokens":495},"completion_tokens_details":{"text_tokens":368}}}